# =============================================================================
# Package: calife
# Description: PAM (Pluggable Authentication Modules) configuration
# =============================================================================
# This template configures the global PAM stack for authentication, account
# validation, and session management. It relies on modular includes to keep
# individual concerns (like password policies or account locking) separate
# and reusable.
#
# Variable Mapping:
# - Since the schema provided is empty, this template assumes the standard
#   Debian/Ubuntu `common-*` PAM stack structure. No custom variables are
#   injected.
# =============================================================================

# --- Authentication Modules ---
# These modules handle the verification of user credentials (passwords, tokens, etc.).
@include common-auth

# --- Account Modules ---
# These modules determine if the user's account is valid, active, and allowed to
# log in at this time (e.g., checking for expired passwords or lockouts).
@include common-account

# --- Session Modules ---
# These modules manage the user's session lifecycle, such as mounting home directories,
# recording login attempts, or setting up environment variables.
# The 'noninteractive' variant is often used for system services that do not have
# an interactive terminal session.
@include common-session-noninteractive
